      "cardType": "Ability",
      "recallCost": 1,
      "rulesText": "When observing a creature, you can make an Instinct Roll against them. On a success, spend a Hope and ask the GM for one set of information about the target from the following options:\n\n  - Their unmarked Hit Points and Stress.\n  - Their Difficulty and damage thresholds.\n  - Their tactics and standard attack damage dice.\n  - Their features and Experiences.\n\nAdditionally on a success, you can mark a Stress to remove a Fear from the GM’s Fear Pool.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/know-thy-enemy/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/lead-by-example",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Lead by Example",
      "slug": "lead-by-example",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "LEAD BY EXAMPLE",
        "lineStart": 16409,
        "lineEnd": 16415,
        "pdfPageStart": 224,
        "pdfPageEnd": 224
      },
      "level": 9,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/valor"
      },
      "cardType": "Ability",
      "recallCost": 3,
      "rulesText": "When you deal damage to an adversary, you can mark a Stress and describe how you encourage your allies. The next PC to make an attack against that adversary can clear a Stress or gain a Hope.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/lead-by-example/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/lean-on-me",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Lean on Me",
      "slug": "lean-on-me",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "LEAN ON ME",
        "lineStart": 16300,
        "lineEnd": 16306,
        "pdfPageStart": 223,
        "pdfPageEnd": 223
      },
      "level": 3,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/valor"
      },
      "cardType": "Ability",
      "recallCost": 1,
      "rulesText": "Once per long rest, when you console or inspire an ally who failed an action roll, you can both clear 2 Stress.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/lean-on-me/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/life-ward",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Life Ward",
      "slug": "life-ward",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "LIFE WARD",
        "lineStart": 16114,
        "lineEnd": 16122,
        "pdfPageStart": 221,
        "pdfPageEnd": 221
      },
      "level": 4,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/splendor"
      },
      "cardType": "Spell",
      "recallCost": 1,
      "rulesText": "Spend 3 Hope and choose an ally within Close range. They are marked with a glowing sigil of protection. When this ally would make a death move, they clear a Hit Point instead.\n\nThis effect ends when it saves the target from a death move, you cast Life Ward on another target, or you take a long rest.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/life-ward/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/manifest-wall",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Manifest Wall",
      "slug": "manifest-wall",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "MANIFEST WALL",
        "lineStart": 15086,
        "lineEnd": 15092,
        "pdfPageStart": 212,
        "pdfPageEnd": 212
      },
      "level": 5,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/codex"
      },
      "cardType": "Spell",
      "recallCost": 2,
      "rulesText": "Make a Spellcast Roll (15). Once per rest on a success, spend a Hope to create a temporary magical wall between two points within Far range. It can be up to 50 feet high and form at any angle. Creatures or objects in its path are shunted to a side of your choice. The wall stays up until your next rest or you cast Manifest Wall again.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/manifest-wall/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/mass-disguise",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Mass Disguise",
      "slug": "mass-disguise",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "MASS DISGUISE",
        "lineStart": 15713,
        "lineEnd": 15721,
        "pdfPageStart": 217,
        "pdfPageEnd": 217
      },
      "level": 6,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/midnight"
      },
      "cardType": "Spell",
      "recallCost": 0,
      "rulesText": "When you have a few minutes of silence to focus, you can mark a Stress to change the appearance of all willing creatures within Close range. Their new forms must share a general body structure and size, and can be somebody or something you’ve seen before or entirely fabricated. A disguised creature has advantage on Presence Rolls to avoid scrutiny.\n\nActivate a Countdown (8). It ticks down as a consequence the GM chooses. When it triggers, the disguise drops.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/mass-disguise/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/mass-enrapture",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Mass Enrapture",
      "slug": "mass-enrapture",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "MASS ENRAPTURE",
        "lineStart": 15576,
        "lineEnd": 15582,
        "pdfPageStart": 216,
        "pdfPageEnd": 216
      },
      "level": 8,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/grace"
      },
      "cardType": "Spell",
      "recallCost": 3,
      "rulesText": "Make a Spellcast Roll against all targets within Far range. Targets you succeed against become temporarily Enraptured. While Enraptured, a target’s attention is fixed on you, narrowing their field of view and drowning out any sound but your voice. Mark a Stress to force all Enraptured targets to mark a Stress, ending this spell.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/mass-enrapture/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/master-of-the-craft",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Master of the Craft",
      "slug": "master-of-the-craft",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "MASTER OF THE CRAFT",
        "lineStart": 15592,
        "lineEnd": 15598,
        "pdfPageStart": 216,
        "pdfPageEnd": 216
      },
      "level": 9,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/grace"
      },
      "cardType": "Ability",
      "recallCost": 0,
      "rulesText": "Gain a permanent +2 bonus to two of your Experiences or a permanent +3 bonus to one of your Experiences. Then place this card in your vault permanently.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/master-of-the-craft/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/mending-touch",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Mending Touch",
      "slug": "mending-touch",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "MENDING TOUCH",
        "lineStart": 16054,
        "lineEnd": 16062,
        "pdfPageStart": 221,
        "pdfPageEnd": 221
      },
      "level": 1,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/splendor"
      },
      "cardType": "Spell",
      "recallCost": 1,
      "rulesText": "You lay your hands upon a creature and channel healing magic to close their wounds. When you can take a few minutes to focus on the target you’re helping, you can spend 2 Hope to clear a Hit Point or a Stress on them.\n\nOnce per long rest, when you spend this healing time learning something new about them or revealing something about yourself, you can clear 2 Hit Points or 2 Stress on them instead.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/mending-touch/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/midnight-spirit",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Midnight Spirit",
      "slug": "midnight-spirit",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "MIDNIGHT SPIRIT",
        "lineStart": 15628,
        "lineEnd": 15636,
        "pdfPageStart": 217,
        "pdfPageEnd": 217
      },
      "level": 2,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/midnight"
      },
      "cardType": "Spell",
      "recallCost": 1,
      "rulesText": "Spend a Hope to summon a humanoid‑sized spirit that can move or carry things for you until your next rest.\n\nYou can also send it to attack an adversary. When you do, make a Spellcast Roll against a target within Very Far range. On a success, the spirit moves into Melee range with that target. Roll a number of d6s equal to your Spellcast trait and deal that much magic damage to the target. The spirit then dissipates. You can only have one spirit at a time.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/midnight-spirit/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/midnight-touched",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Midnight‑touched",
      "slug": "midnight-touched",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "MIDNIGHT‑TOUCHED",
        "lineStart": 15723,
        "lineEnd": 15733,
        "pdfPageStart": 217,
        "pdfPageEnd": 217
      },
      "level": 7,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/midnight"
      },
      "cardType": "Ability",
      "recallCost": 2,
      "rulesText": "When 4 or more of the domain cards in your loadout are from the Midnight domain, gain the following benefits:\n\n  - Once per rest, when you have 0 Hope and the GM would gain a Fear, you can gain a Hope instead.\n\n  - When you make a successful attack, you can mark a Stress to add the result of your Fear Die to your damage roll.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/midnight-touched/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/natural-familiar",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Natural Familiar",
      "slug": "natural-familiar",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "NATURAL FAMILIAR",
        "lineStart": 15850,
        "lineEnd": 15858,
        "pdfPageStart": 219,
        "pdfPageEnd": 219
      },
      "level": 2,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/sage"
      },
      "cardType": "Spell",
      "recallCost": 1,
      "rulesText": "Spend a Hope to summon a small nature spirit or forest critter to your side until your next rest, you cast Natural Familiar again, or the familiar is targeted by an attack. If you spend an additional Hope, you can summon a familiar that flies. You can communicate with them, make a Spellcast Roll to command them to perform simple tasks, and mark a Stress to see through their eyes.\n\nWhen you deal damage to an adversary within Melee range of your familiar, you add a d6 to your damage roll.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/natural-familiar/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/natures-tongue",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Nature’s Tongue",
      "slug": "natures-tongue",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "NATURE’S TONGUE",
        "lineStart": 15818,
        "lineEnd": 15826,
        "pdfPageStart": 218,
        "pdfPageEnd": 218
      },
      "level": 1,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/sage"
      },
      "cardType": "Ability",
      "recallCost": 0,
      "rulesText": "You can speak the language of the natural world. When you want to speak to the plants and animals around you, make an Instinct Roll (12). On a success, they’ll give you the information they know. On a roll with Fear, their knowledge might be limited or come at a cost.\n\nAdditionally, before you make a Spellcast Roll while within a natural environment, you can spend a Hope to gain a +2 bonus to the roll.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/natures-tongue/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/never-upstaged",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Never Upstaged",
      "slug": "never-upstaged",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "NEVER UPSTAGED",
        "lineStart": 15507,
        "lineEnd": 15513,
        "pdfPageStart": 215,
        "pdfPageEnd": 215
      },
      "level": 6,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/grace"
      },
      "cardType": "Ability",
      "recallCost": 2,
      "rulesText": "When you mark 1 or more Hit Points from an attack, you can mark a Stress to place a number of tokens equal to the number of Hit Points you marked on this card. On your next successful attack, gain a +5 bonus to your damage roll for each token on this card, then clear all tokens.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/never-upstaged/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/night-terror",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Night Terror",
      "slug": "night-terror",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "NIGHT TERROR",
        "lineStart": 15763,
        "lineEnd": 15769,
        "pdfPageStart": 218,
        "pdfPageEnd": 218
      },
      "level": 9,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/midnight"
      },
      "cardType": "Spell",
      "recallCost": 2,
      "rulesText": "Once per long rest, choose any targets within Very Close range to perceive you as a nightmarish horror. The targets must succeed on a Reaction Roll (16) or become temporarily Horrified. While Horrified, they’re Vulnerable. Steal a number of Fear from the GM equal to the number of targets that are Horrified (up to the number of Fear in the GM’s pool). Roll a number of d6s equal to the number of stolen Fear and deal the total damage to each Horrified target. Discard the stolen Fear.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/night-terror/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/not-good-enough",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Not Good Enough",
      "slug": "not-good-enough",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "NOT GOOD ENOUGH",
        "lineStart": 14595,
        "lineEnd": 14601,
        "pdfPageStart": 208,
        "pdfPageEnd": 208
      },
      "level": 1,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/blade"
      },
      "cardType": "Ability",
      "recallCost": 1,
      "rulesText": "When you roll your damage dice, you can reroll any 1s or 2s.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/not-good-enough/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/notorious",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Notorious",
      "slug": "notorious",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "NOTORIOUS",
        "lineStart": 15608,
        "lineEnd": 15614,
        "pdfPageStart": 216,
        "pdfPageEnd": 216
      },
      "level": 10,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/grace"
      },
      "cardType": "Ability",
      "recallCost": 0,
      "rulesText": "People know who you are and what you’ve done, and they treat you differently because of it. When you leverage your notoriety to get what you want, you can mark a Stress before you roll to gain a +10 bonus to the result. Your food and drinks are always free wherever you go, and everything else you buy is reduced in price by one bag of gold (to a minimum of one handful).",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/notorious/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/on-the-brink",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "On the Brink",
      "slug": "on-the-brink",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "ON THE BRINK",
        "lineStart": 14942,
        "lineEnd": 14948,
        "pdfPageStart": 210,
        "pdfPageEnd": 210
      },
      "level": 9,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/bone"
      },
      "cardType": "Ability",
      "recallCost": 1,
      "rulesText": "When you have 2 or fewer Hit Points unmarked, you don’t take Minor damage.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/on-the-brink/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/onslaught",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Onslaught",
      "slug": "onslaught",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "ONSLAUGHT",
        "lineStart": 14808,
        "lineEnd": 14816,
        "pdfPageStart": 209,
        "pdfPageEnd": 209
      },
      "level": 10,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/blade"
      },
      "cardType": "Ability",
      "recallCost": 3,
      "rulesText": "When you successfully make an attack with your weapon, you never deal damage beneath a target’s Major damage threshold (the target always marks a minimum of 2 Hit Points).\n\nAdditionally, when a creature within your weapon’s range deals damage to an ally with an attack that doesn’t include you, you can mark a Stress to force them to make a Reaction Roll (15). On a failure, the target must mark a Hit Point.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/onslaught/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/overwhelming-aura",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Overwhelming Aura",
      "slug": "overwhelming-aura",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "OVERWHELMING AURA",
        "lineStart": 16218,
        "lineEnd": 16226,
        "pdfPageStart": 222,
        "pdfPageEnd": 222
      },
      "level": 9,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/splendor"
      },
      "cardType": "Spell",
      "recallCost": 2,
      "rulesText": "Make a Spellcast Roll (15) to magically empower your aura. On a success, spend 2 Hope to make your Presence equal to your Spellcast trait until your next long rest.\n\nWhile this spell is active, an adversary must mark a Stress when they target you with an attack.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/overwhelming-aura/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domain-cards/phantom-retreat",
      "@type": "DomainCard",
      "name": "Phantom Retreat",
      "slug": "phantom-retreat",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "PHANTOM RETREAT",
        "lineStart": 15692,
        "lineEnd": 15698,
        "pdfPageStart": 217,
        "pdfPageEnd": 217
      },
      "level": 5,
      "domain": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/domains/midnight"
      },
      "cardType": "Spell",
      "recallCost": 2,
      "rulesText": "Spend a Hope to activate Phantom Retreat where you’re currently standing. Spend another Hope at any time before your next rest to disappear from where you are and reappear where you were standing when you activated Phantom Retreat. This spell ends after you reappear.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/domain-cards/phantom-retreat/"
      },
      "source": {
