    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/adversaries-by-tier",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Adversaries by Tier",
      "slug": "adversaries-by-tier",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "RUNNING AN ADVENTURE",
        "heading": "ADVERSARIES BY TIER",
        "lineStart": 5067,
        "lineEnd": 5348,
        "pdfPageStart": 95,
        "pdfPageEnd": 96
      },
      "rulesText": "This section contains the following stat blocks:\n\n##### TIER 1 (LEVEL 1)\n\n- Acid Burrower\n- Ahuizotl\n- Atototl\n- Bear\n- Bugboar\n- Cave Ogre\n- Common Ruffian\n- Construct\n- Courtier\n- Darkweave Crawler\n- Darkweave Queen\n- Darkweave Spinner\n- Darkweave Swarmlings\n- Deeproot Defender\n- Dire Wolf\n- Elk\n- Falcon\n- Giant Mosquitoes\n- Giant Rat\n- Giant Scorpion\n- Glass Snake\n- Grimmling Warband\n- Archer Guard\n- Bladed Guard\n- Head Guard\n- Harpy\n- Harrier\n- Jagged Knife Bandit\n- Jagged Knife Hexer\n- Jagged Knife Kneebreaker\n- Jagged Knife Lackey\n- Jagged Knife Lieutenant\n- Jagged Knife Shadow\n- Jagged Knife Sniper\n- Kelpie\n- Masque Muerte\n- Mechanorb\n- Merchant\n- Minor Chaos Elemental\n- Minor Fire Elemental\n- Minor Demon\n- Minor Treant\n- Mountain Troll\n- Octopus\n- Green Ooze\n- Tiny Green Ooze\n- Red Ooze\n- Tiny Red Ooze\n- Panther\n- Petty Noble\n- Phantom\n- Pirate Captain\n- Pirate Raiders\n- Pirate Tough\n- Poltergeist\n- Rabble Mawb\n- Redcap Biters\n- Redcap Breaker\n- Redcap Butcher\n- Redcap Candlemaker\n- Redcap Skinner\n- Rugaru\n- Sawtoothed Gillbeast\n- Sellsword\n- Skeleton Archer\n- Skeleton Dredge\n- Skeleton Knight\n- Skeleton Warrior\n- Soul-Shattered Mage\n- Spellblade\n- Spellbound Armor\n- Swarm of Rats\n- Sylvan Soldier\n- Tangle Bramble Swarm\n- Tangle Bramble\n- Viper\n- Waxwork Creation\n- Weaponmaster\n- Will-o’-the-Wisps\n- Young Dryad\n- Yufo\n- Brawny Zombie\n- Patchwork Zombie Hulk\n- Rotted Zombie\n- Shambling Zombie\n- Zombie Pack\n\n##### TIER 2 (LEVELS 2–4)\n\n- Archer Squadron\n- Apprentice Assassin\n- Assassin Poisoner\n- Master Assassin\n- Banshee\n- Basilisk\n- Battle Box\n- Berserker Alpha\n- Berserker Initiate\n- Centaur Warden\n- Chaos Skull\n- Chicken-Foot Hut\n- Conscript\n- Courtesan\n- Cult Adept\n- Cult Fang\n- Cult Initiate\n- Demonic Hound Pack\n- Dire Pangolati\n- Doppelhound\n- Dragon Knight\n- Electric Eels\n- Elephant\n- Elite Soldier\n- Entombed Cat Beast\n- Entombed Elite Guard\n- Entombed Empress\n- Entombed Necropriest\n- Entombed Skin Beetles\n\n- Entombed Stonemason\n- Failed Experiment\n- Flock of Feather Fiends\n- Fowlbear\n- Fungispunj Sporeling\n- Fungispunj Sporophore\n- Gargoyle\n- Giant Beastmaster\n- Giant Brawler\n- Giant Eagle\n- Giant Octopus\n- Giant Recruit\n- Gobstalker\n- Gorgon\n- Guahalan Alebrujo\n- Guahalan Fang Lord\n- Guahalan Shifter\n- Guahalan Spirit Beast\n- Guahalan Spirit Singer\n- Hill Titan\n- Hive Walker\n- Jack-o’-Lantern\n- Juvenile Flickerfly\n- Knight of the Realm\n- Landshark\n- Landshark Behemoth\n- Masked Thief\n- Merchant Baron\n- Minotaur Wrecker\n- Mortal Hunter\n- Ravenous Mockery\n- Royal Advisor\n- Rust Eater\n- Scarecrow\n- Secret-Keeper\n- Shark\n- Siren\n- Spectral Archer\n- Spectral Captain\n- Spectral Guardian\n- Sprite\n- Spy\n- Stone Titan\n- Stonewraith\n- Triceratops\n- Tyrannosaurus\n- Urco\n- Valdenhax\n- War Wizard\n\n##### TIER 3 (LEVELS 5–7)\n\n- Adult Flickerfly\n- Archmage\n- Catrin\n- Chimera\n- Crimson Lepus\n- Cryptimoth\n- Cursed Merfolk\n- Deep Dweller\n- Demon of Avarice\n- Demon of Despair\n- Demon of Hubris\n- Demon of Jealousy\n- Demon of Wrath\n- Dire Bat\n- Drake\n- Dryad\n- Dullahan\n- Elemental Spark\n- Fellmounted Shadow King\n- Fire Titan\n- Frost Titan\n- Gargantuan Sea Turtle\n- Greater Earth Elemental\n- Greater Water Elemental\n- Huge Green Ooze\n- Hydra\n- Lamia\n- Lamplight Beguiler\n- Manticore\n- Monarch\n- Night Children\n- Pain Priest\n- Phoenix\n- Plesiosaurus\n- Roc\n- Sandwyrm\n- Shapeshifting Fiend\n- Shapeshifting Fiend Revealed\n- Stag Knight\n- Storm Titan\n- Oak Treant\n- Treant Sapling\n- Unicorn\n- Head Vampire\n- Vampire\n- Vampire Bat Swarm\n- Vampire Lord\n- Vault Guardian Gaoler\n- Vault Guardian Sentinel\n- Vault Guardian Turret\n- Viscera Sucker\n- Whisper Wraith\n- Wyvern\n- Young Fire Dragon\n- Young Ice Dragon\n\n##### TIER 4 (LEVELS 8–10)\n\n- Arch-Necromancer\n- Cephilith Abomination\n- Cephilith Hatchling\n- Cephilith Novitiate\n- Cephilith Priest\n- Cephilith Titan\n- Cipactli\n- Cloud Titan\n- Demon Lord Berzug\n- Dragon Mother Mitera\n- Fallen Shock Troop\n- Fallen Sorcerer\n- Fallen Warlord: Realm-Breaker\n- Fallen Warlord: Undefeated Champion\n- Fire Titan Warlord\n- Gargantuan War Machine\n- Ghastly Legion\n- Griffin\n- Hallowed Archer\n- Hallowed Choir\n- Hallowed Soldier\n- Harbinger of Death\n- Harbinger of Famine\n- Harbinger of Pestilence\n- Harbinger of War\n- High Seraph\n- Kraken\n- Oracle of Doom\n- Outer Realms Abomination\n- Outer Realms Corruptor\n- Outer Realms Thrall\n- Owl Witch\n- Ruby Dragon\n- Severed Shadow\n- Supreme Demiurge Adonix\n- Temporal Enforcer\n- Volcanic Dragon: Obsidian Predator\n- Volcanic Dragon: Molten Scourge\n- Volcanic Dragon: Ashen Tyrant\n- Water Mother\n- Wyrmfiend\n- Wyrmlings\n- Xero the Castle Killer\n- Perfected Zombie\n- Zombie Legion",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/adversaries-by-tier/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/adversary-attack-rolls",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Adversary Attack Rolls",
      "slug": "adversary-attack-rolls",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "RUNNING AN ADVENTURE",
        "heading": "ADVERSARY ATTACK ROLLS",
        "lineStart": 4495,
        "lineEnd": 4501,
        "pdfPageStart": 86,
        "pdfPageEnd": 86
      },
      "rulesText": "When an adversary attacks a PC, roll your d20 and add the adversary’s attack bonus to the result. If the total meets or beats the target’s Evasion, the attack succeeds; otherwise, the attack fails. On a successful attack, roll the attack’s damage dice to determine how much it deals.\n\nIf you roll a natural 20 on an attack, your roll automatically succeeds and you deal extra damage. Roll damage normally, then add the highest number on the damage dice to the total. For example, an attack that deals 3d6+2 deals 18+3d6+2 on a critical success; the critical success does not affect the flat damage modifier.\n\n> Note: a critical success on an adversary’s reaction roll automatically succeeds, but confers no additional benefit.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/adversary-attack-rolls/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/adversary-stat-block-benchmarks",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Adversary Stat Block Benchmarks",
      "slug": "adversary-stat-block-benchmarks",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "RUNNING AN ADVENTURE",
        "heading": "ADVERSARY STAT BLOCK BENCHMARKS",
        "lineStart": 5058,
        "lineEnd": 5065,
        "pdfPageStart": 95,
        "pdfPageEnd": 95
      },
      "rulesText": "| Adversary Statistic | Tier 1 | Tier 2 | Tier 3 | Tier 4 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Attack Modifier | +1 | +2 | +3 | +4 |\n| Damage Dice | 1d6+2 to 1d12+4 | 2d6+3 to 2d12+4 | 3d8+3 to 3d12+5 | 4d8+10 to 4d12+15 |\n| Difficulty | 11 | 14 | 17 | 20 |\n| Damage Thresholds | Major 7/Severe 12 | Major 10/Severe 20 | Major 20/Severe 32 | Major 25/Severe 45 |",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/adversary-stat-block-benchmarks/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/adversary-stat-blocks",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Adversary Stat Blocks",
      "slug": "adversary-stat-blocks",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "RUNNING AN ADVENTURE",
        "heading": "ADVERSARY STAT BLOCKS",
        "lineStart": 4895,
        "lineEnd": 4935,
        "pdfPageStart": 93,
        "pdfPageEnd": 93
      },
      "rulesText": "All the information required to run an adversary is contained in their stat block. An adversary’s stat block includes their:\n\n##### NAME\n\nEach stat block has a unique name. Abilities that affect adversaries with a certain name include all adversaries who use that stat block, regardless of their in-story name.\n\n##### TIER\n\nEach adversary is designed to oppose PCs of a certain tier. If you confront the party with an adversary from another tier, adjust their stats.\n\n##### TYPE\n\nThe adversary’s type appears alongside their tier. An adversary’s type represents the role they play in a conflict. The adversary types are:\n\n- **Bruisers:** tough; deliver powerful attacks.\n- **Hordes:** groups of identical creatures acting together as a single unit.\n\n> Note: The number of creatures represented by each Hit Point in a horde's stat block is indicated by \"X/HP.\" For example, a 2/HP horde with 3 HP represents a group of six.\n\n- **Leaders:** command and summon other adversaries.\n- **Minions:** easily dispatched but dangerous in numbers.\n- **Ranged:** fragile in close encounters but deal high damage at range.\n- **Skulks:** maneuver and exploit opportunities to ambush opponents.\n- **Socials:** present challenges around conversation instead of combat.\n- **Solos:** present a formidable challenge to a whole party, with or without support.\n- **Standards:** representative of their fictional group.\n- **Supports:** enhance their allies and disrupt their opponents.\n\n##### DESCRIPTION\n\nA summary of the adversary's appearance and demeanor.\n\n##### MOTIVES & TACTICS\n\nSuggusted impulses, actions and goals for the adversary.\n\n##### DIFFICULTY\n\nThe Difficulty of any roll made against the adversary, unless otherwise noted.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/adversary-stat-blocks/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/agile-scout",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Agile Scout",
      "slug": "agile-scout",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "AGILE SCOUT",
        "lineStart": 855,
        "lineEnd": 867,
        "pdfPageStart": 15,
        "pdfPageEnd": 15
      },
      "rulesText": "*(Fox, Mouse, Weasel, etc.)*\n\n*Agility +1 | Evasion +2*\n\n*Melee Agility d4 phy*\n\n**Gain advantage on:** deceive, locate, sneak\n\n**Agile:** Your movement is silent, and you can spend a Hope to move up to Far range without rolling.\n\n**Fragile:** When you take Major or greater damage, you drop out of Beastform.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/agile-scout/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/ancestries",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Ancestries",
      "slug": "ancestries",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "ANCESTRIES",
        "lineStart": 2137,
        "lineEnd": 2145,
        "pdfPageStart": 32,
        "pdfPageEnd": 32
      },
      "rulesText": "Ancestries represent your character’s lineage, which affects their physical appearance and access to certain special abilities. The following section describes each ancestry in Daggerheart and the characteristics generally shared by members of that ancestry, however, each player decides how much their character aligns with the “standard” or “average” expression of their ancestry.\n\nIn Daggerheart, the term “people” is used to refer to all ancestries, as individuals from all lineages possess unique characteristics and cultures, as well as personhood.\n\nSome ancestries are described using the term “humanoid.” This does not imply any genetic relation to “humans,” which is a distinct ancestry within Daggerheart. Instead, it refers to the set of physical characteristics humans will recognize from their own anatomy, such as bipedal movement, upright posture, facial layout, and more. These traits vary by ancestry and individual, though “humanoid” should still provide a useful frame of reference.\n\nThe Daggerheart Core Set includes only the following ancestries: Clank, Drakona, Dwarf, Elf, Faerie, Faun, Firbolg, Fungril, Galapa, Giant, Goblin, Halfling, Human, Infernis, Katari, Orc, Ribbet, Simiah, and Mixed Ancestry.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/ancestries/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/ancestry-feature",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Ancestry Feature",
      "slug": "ancestry-feature",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "ANCESTRY FEATURE",
        "lineStart": 2281,
        "lineEnd": 2285,
        "pdfPageStart": 35,
        "pdfPageEnd": 35
      },
      "rulesText": "**Luckbender:** Once per session, after you or a willing ally within Close range makes an action roll, you can spend 3 Hope to reroll the Duality Dice.\n\n**Wings:** You can fly. While flying, you can mark a Stress after an adversary makes an attack against you to gain a +2 bonus to your Evasion against that attack.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/ancestry-feature/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/ancestry-features",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Ancestry Features",
      "slug": "ancestry-features",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "ANCESTRY FEATURES",
        "lineStart": 2147,
        "lineEnd": 2151,
        "pdfPageStart": 32,
        "pdfPageEnd": 32
      },
      "rulesText": "Each ancestry grants two ancestry features. While some features (such as the ability to fly) are implicitly tied to an ancestry’s anatomy, players determine their characters’ physical form. Work with the GM to re-flavor any implied traits that don’t align with your character concept.\n\nIf you’d like to make a character who combines more than one ancestry, see “Mixed Ancestry.”",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/ancestry-features/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/appendix",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Appendix",
      "slug": "appendix",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "APPENDIX",
        "lineStart": 14390,
        "lineEnd": 14392,
        "pdfPageStart": 206,
        "pdfPageEnd": 206
      },
      "rulesText": "This section contains additional information and reference material. For additional reference sheets, visit daggerheart.com/downloads.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/appendix/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/aquatic-predator",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Aquatic Predator",
      "slug": "aquatic-predator",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "AQUATIC PREDATOR",
        "lineStart": 1073,
        "lineEnd": 1085,
        "pdfPageStart": 17,
        "pdfPageEnd": 17
      },
      "rulesText": "*(Dolphin, Orca, Shark, etc.)*\n\n*Agility +2 | Evasion +4*\n\n*Melee Agility d10+6 phy*\n\n**Gain advantage on:** attack, swim, track\n\n**Aquatic:** You can breathe and move naturally underwater.\n\n**Vicious Maul:** When you succeed on an attack against a target, you can spend a Hope to make them Vulnerable and gain a +1 bonus to your Proficiency for this attack.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/aquatic-predator/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/aquatic-scout",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Aquatic Scout",
      "slug": "aquatic-scout",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "AQUATIC SCOUT",
        "lineStart": 913,
        "lineEnd": 925,
        "pdfPageStart": 16,
        "pdfPageEnd": 16
      },
      "rulesText": "*(Eel, Fish, Octopus, etc.)*\n\n*Agility +1 | Evasion +2*\n\n*Melee Agility d4 phy*\n\n**Gain advantage on:** navigate, sneak, swim\n\n**Aquatic:** You can breathe and move naturally underwater.\n\n**Fragile:** When you take Major or greater damage, you drop out of Beastform.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/aquatic-scout/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/arcana-domain",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Arcana Domain",
      "slug": "arcana-domain",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "ARCANA DOMAIN",
        "lineStart": 14396,
        "lineEnd": 14396,
        "pdfPageStart": 206,
        "pdfPageEnd": 206
      },
      "rulesText": "",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/arcana-domain/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/arcane-hold",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Arcane Hold",
      "slug": "arcane-hold",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "RUNNING AN ADVENTURE",
        "heading": "ARCANE HOLD",
        "lineStart": 4809,
        "lineEnd": 4815,
        "pdfPageStart": 91,
        "pdfPageEnd": 91
      },
      "rulesText": "**Choice:** When the battle begins, choose a favored PC.\n\n**Trigger:** The first time during a battle the favored PC is within Close range and hit with an attack.\n\n**Effect:** Make an attack roll with a +6 modifier against the adversary. On a success, the target is temporarily Restrained by tendrils of powerful magic.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/arcane-hold/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/armor",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Armor",
      "slug": "armor",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MECHANICS",
        "heading": "ARMOR",
        "lineStart": 3905,
        "lineEnd": 4015,
        "pdfPageStart": 72,
        "pdfPageEnd": 74
      },
      "rulesText": "Every armor has a name, base damage thresholds, and a base Armor Score. Some armor also has a feature.\n\n- An armor’s base armor score indicates how many Armor Slots it provides its wearer before additional bonuses are added to calculate their total Armor Score. A PC’s Armor Score can’t exceed 12.\n- An armor’s base thresholds determine its wearer’s Major and Severe damage thresholds before adding bonuses to calculate their final damage thresholds. When recording your character’s damage thresholds in the “Damage & Health” section of your character sheet, you always add your character’s level to those values.\n- An armor’s feature is a special rule that stays in effect while the armor is equipped.\n\nWhile unarmored, your character’s base Armor Score is 0, their Major threshold is equal to their level, and their Severe threshold is equal to twice their level.\n\n##### REDUCING INCOMING DAMAGE\n\nWhen you take damage, you can mark one Armor Slot to reduce the severity of the damage by one threshold (Severe to Major, Major to Minor, Minor to nothing). If your character has an Armor Score of 0, you can’t mark Armor Slots. If an effect temporarily increases your Armor Score, it increases your available Armor Slots by the same amount; when the effect ends, so does the availability of these Armor Slots.\n\n#### ARMOR TABLES\n\n##### TIER 1 (LEVEL 1)\n\n| Name | Base Thresholds | Base Score | Feature |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Mage Robes | 4 / 10 | 2 | Enchanted: Gain a bonus to your damage thresholds equal to your Spellcast trait. |\n| Gambeson Armor | 5 / 11 | 3 | Flexible: +1 to Evasion |\n| Brigandine Armor | 6 / 12 | 3 | Lined: Mark a Stress to negate Minor damage. |\n| Leather Armor | 6 / 13 | 3 | — |\n| Scale Mail Armor | 7 / 14 | 3 | Cumbersome: −1 to Finesse |\n| Chainmail Armor | 7 / 15 | 4 | Heavy: −1 to Evasion |\n| Banded Armor | 8 / 16 | 4 | Bulky: −1 to Evasion; when you take Severe damage, you must mark a Stress. |\n| Full Plate Armor | 8 / 17 | 4 | Very Heavy: −2 to Evasion; −1 to Agility |\n\n##### TIER 2 (LEVELS 2–4)\n\n| Name | Base Thresholds | Base Score | Feature |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Improved Mage Robes | 6 / 15 | 3 | Enchanted: Gain a bonus to your damage thresholds equal to your Spellcast trait. |\n| Improved Gambeson Armor | 7 / 16 | 4 | Flexible: +1 to Evasion |\n| Improved Brigandine Armor | 9 / 19 | 4 | Lined: Mark a Stress to negate Minor damage. |\n| Improved Leather Armor | 9 / 20 | 4 | — |\n| Improved Scale Mail Armor | 11 / 23 | 4 | Cumbersome: −1 to Finesse |\n| Improved Chainmail Armor | 11 / 24 | 5 | Heavy: −1 to Evasion |\n| Improved Banded Armor | 13 / 27 | 5 | Bulky: −1 to Evasion; when you take Severe damage, you must mark a Stress. |\n| Improved Full Plate Armor | 13 / 28 | 5 | Very Heavy: −2 to Evasion; −1 to Agility |\n| Enchanter’s Robes | 9 / 20 | 4 | Mnemonic: Once per scene, you can recall a domain card from your vault without paying its Recall Cost. |\n| Hawkguard’s Mantle | 9 / 20 | 4 | Gliding: You can glide up to Far range and are immune to damage from falling. |\n| Spidersilk Tunic | 9 / 20 | 4 | Wall-Crawling: +1 Evasion; you can walk on walls as easily as on the ground. |\n\n| | | | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Stormthread Habit | 9 / 20 | 4 | Absorbing: Once per scene when you take magic damage, you can clear an Armor Slot. |\n| Elundrian Chain Armor | 9 / 21 | 4 | Warded: You reduce incoming magic damage by your Armor Score before applying it to your damage thresholds. |\n| Harrowbone Armor | 9 / 21 | 4 | Resilient: Before you mark your last Armor Slot, roll a d6. On a result of 6, reduce the severity by one threshold without marking an Armor Slot. |\n| Irontree Breastplate Armor | 9 / 20 | 4 | Reinforced: When you mark your last Armor Slot, increase your damage thresholds by +2 until you clear at least 1 Armor Slot. |\n| Runetan Floating Armor | 9 / 20 | 4 | Shifting: When you are targeted for an attack, you can mark an Armor Slot to give the attack roll against you disadvantage. |\n| Tyris Soft Armor | 8 / 18 | 5 | Quiet: You gain a +2 bonus to rolls you make to move silently. |\n| Wyrdwood Splint Armor | 10 / 21 | 5 | Quick-Striding: You can’t be Restrained and can move up to Far range as part of an action roll. |\n| Rosewild Armor | 11 / 23 | 5 | Hopeful: When you would spend a Hope, you can mark an Armor Slot instead. |\n| Trollhide Cuirass | 11 / 23 | 5 | Self-Healing: When you take a rest, clear an Armor Slot. |\n| Gilded Sunplate | 12 / 26 | 5 | Resplendent: Once per scene when you spend Hope, you can clear an Armor Slot. |\n\n##### TIER 3 (LEVELS 5–7)\n\n| Name | Base Thresholds | Base Score | Feature |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Advanced Mage Robes | 8 / 22 | 4 | Enchanted: Gain a bonus to your damage thresholds equal to your Spellcast trait. |\n| Advanced Gambeson Armor | 9 / 23 | 5 | Flexible: +1 to Evasion |\n| Advanced Brigandine Armor | 11 / 26 | 5 | Lined: Mark a Stress to negate Minor damage. |\n| Advanced Leather Armor | 11 / 27 | 5 | — |\n| Advanced Scale Mail Armor | 13 / 30 | 5 | Cumbersome: −1 to Finesse |\n| Advanced Chainmail Armor | 13 / 31 | 6 | Heavy: −1 to Evasion |\n| Advanced Banded Armor | 15 / 34 | 6 | Bulky: −1 to Evasion; when you take Severe damage, you must mark a Stress. |\n| Advanced Full Plate Armor | 15 / 35 | 6 | Very Heavy: −2 to Evasion; −1 to Agility |\n| Granminster’s Finery | 11 / 27 | 2 | Magnificent: Gain a bonus to your Armor Score equal to your Presence. |\n| Spiked Plate Armor | 10 / 25 | 5 | Sharp: On a successful attack against a target within Melee range, add a d4 to the damage roll. |\n| Astral Raiment | 11 / 27 | 5 | Stellar: Mark a Stress to gain advantage on a Spellcast roll. |\n| Bellamoi Fine Armor | 11 / 27 | 5 | Gilded: +1 to Presence |\n| Cloverweave Cloak | 11 / 27 | 5 | Fortune-Favored: Once per scene, you can change a failure with Hope into a success with Fear. |\n| Dragonscale Armor | 11 / 27 | 5 | Impenetrable: Once per short rest, when you would mark your last Hit Point, you can instead mark a Stress. |\n| Skywarden’s Lamellar | 11 / 27 | 5 | Vigilant: +2 to Evasion |\n| Bloodstone Plate Armor | 13 / 35 | 6 | Bloodthirsty: When you critically succeed on a weapon attack within Melee range, clear a Hit Point. |\n| Deep-Forged Coral Armor | 13 / 35 | 6 | Aquatic: You can breathe underwater and gain advantage on Agility Rolls while submerged. |\n| Bladefare Armor | 16 / 39 | 6 | Physical: You can’t mark an Armor Slot to reduce magic damage. |\n| Monett’s Cloak | 16 / 39 | 6 | Magic: You can’t mark an Armor Slot to reduce physical damage. |\n| Runes of Fortification | 17 / 43 | 6 | Painful: Each time you mark an Armor Slot, you must mark a Stress. |\n\n##### TIER 4 (LEVELS 8–10)\n\n| Name | Base Thresholds | Base Score | Feature |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Legendary Mage Robes | 10 / 31 | 5 | Enchanted: Gain a bonus to your damage thresholds equal to your Spellcast trait. |\n| Legendary Gambeson Armor | 11 / 32 | 6 | Flexible: +1 to Evasion |\n| Legendary Brigandine Armor | 13 / 35 | 6 | Lined: Mark a Stress to negate Minor damage. |\n| Legendary Leather Armor | 13 / 36 | 6 | — |\n| Legendary Scale Mail Armor | 15 / 39 | 6 | Cumbersome: −1 to Finesse |\n| Legendary Chainmail Armor | 15 / 40 | 7 | Heavy: −1 to Evasion |\n| Legendary Banded Armor | 17 / 43 | 7 | Bulky: −1 to Evasion; when you take Severe damage, you must mark a Stress. |\n| Legendary Full Plate Armor | 17 / 44 | 7 | Very Heavy: −2 to Evasion; −1 to Agility |\n| Full Fortified Armor | 15 / 40 | 4 | Fortified: When you mark an Armor Slot, you reduce the severity of an attack by two thresholds instead of one. |\n| Channeling Armor | 13 / 36 | 5 | Channeling: +1 to Spellcast Rolls |\n| Darkweave Shroud | 13 / 36 | 5 | Ghostwalker: Once per rest, mark a Stress to move up to Close range through solid objects. |\n| Emberwoven Armor | 13 / 36 | 6 | Burning: When an adversary attacks you within Melee range, they mark a Stress. |\n| Godbound Laminar | 13 / 36 | 6 | Divine: When you mark an Armor Slot, gain a Hope. |\n| Veritas Opal Armor | 13 / 36 | 6 | Truthseeking: This armor glows when another creature within Close range tells a lie. |\n| Circle-Forged Dreadplate | 14 / 38 | 6 | Accursed: When you mark any number of Hit Points from an attack, roll a d4. On a result of 4, the attacker must mark an equal number of Stress. |\n| Rune-Forged Exosuit | 12 / 39 | 7 | Attuned: The maximum number of domain cards in your loadout is reduced by one, but you gain a bonus to your damage thresholds equal to your tier. |\n| Dunamis Silkchain | 13 / 36 | 7 | Timeslowing: Mark an Armor Slot to roll a d4 and add its result as a bonus to your Evasion against an incoming attack. |\n| Hallowed Heroplate | 13 / 35 | 7 | Blessed: Once per long rest, you can spend any number of Hope before you make the Risk It All death move. You gain a bonus to the result of your Hope Die equal to the number of Hope spent. |\n| Resonant Harness | 15 / 40 | 7 | Vitreous: When you would take Severe or greater damage, you can mark 2 Armor Slots to negate that damage. If you do, you gain a −5 penalty to your damage thresholds until you choose to repair your armor as a downtime move. |\n| Savior Chainmail | 18 / 48 | 8 | Difficult: −1 to all character traits and Evasion |",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/armor/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/armored-sentry",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Armored Sentry",
      "slug": "armored-sentry",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "ARMORED SENTRY",
        "lineStart": 943,
        "lineEnd": 955,
        "pdfPageStart": 16,
        "pdfPageEnd": 16
      },
      "rulesText": "*(Armadillo, Pangolin, Turtle, etc.)*\n\n*Strength +1 | Evasion +1*\n\n*Melee Strength d8+2 phy*\n\n**Gain advantage on:** dig, locate, protect\n\n**Armored Shell:** Your hardened exterior gives you resistance to physical damage. Additionally, mark an Armor Slot to retract into your shell. While in your shell, physical damage is reduced by a number equal to your Armor Score (after applying resistance), but you can’t perform other actions without leaving this form.\n\n**Cannonball:** Mark a Stress to allow an ally to throw or launch you at an adversary. To do so, the ally makes an attack roll using Agility or Strength (their choice) against a target within Close range. On a success, the adversary takes d12+2 physical damage using the thrower’s Proficiency. You can spend a Hope to target an additional adversary within Very Close range of the first. The second target takes half the damage dealt to the first target.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/armored-sentry/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/assassin-subclasses",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Assassin Subclasses",
      "slug": "assassin-subclasses",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "ASSASSIN SUBCLASSES",
        "lineStart": 398,
        "lineEnd": 400,
        "pdfPageStart": 9,
        "pdfPageEnd": 9
      },
      "rulesText": "Choose either the Executioners Guild or Poisoners Guild subclass.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/assassin-subclasses/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/attacking",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Attacking",
      "slug": "attacking",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MECHANICS",
        "heading": "ATTACKING",
        "lineStart": 3075,
        "lineEnd": 3121,
        "pdfPageStart": 50,
        "pdfPageEnd": 51
      },
      "rulesText": "#### ATTACK ROLLS\n\nAn attack roll is an action roll intended to inflict harm. The trait that applies to an attack roll is specified by the weapon or spell being used. Unarmed attack rolls use either Strength or Finesse (GM’s choice). An attack roll’s Difficulty, unless otherwise noted, is equal to the Difficulty score of its target.\n\n#### DAMAGE ROLLS\n\nOn a successful attack, roll damage. Damage is calculated from the damage roll listed in the attack’s description with the format “xdy+[modifier]” (e.g., for a spell that inflicts “1d8+2” damage, you roll an eight-sided and add 2 to the result; the damage dealt is equal to the total).\n\nAny time an effect says to deal damage using your Spellcast trait, you roll a number of dice equal to your Spellcast trait.\n\n> Note: If your Spellcast trait is +0 or lower, you don’t roll anything.\n\nFor weapons, the number of damage dice you roll is equal to your Proficiency. Note that your Proficiency multiplies the number of dice you roll, but doesn’t affect the modifier. For example, a PC with Proficiency 2 and wielding a weapon with a damage rating of “d8+2” deals damage equal to “2d8+2” on a successful attack.\n\nSuccessful unarmed attacks inflict [Proficiency]d4 damage.\n\n#### CRITICAL DAMAGE\n\nWhen you get a critical success (i.e., you roll matching values on your Duality Dice) on an attack roll, you deal extra damage. Make the damage roll as usual, but add the maximum possible result of the damage dice to the final total. For instance, if an attack would normally deal 2d8+1 damage, a critical success would deal 2d8+1+16.\n\n#### DAMAGE TYPES\n\nThere are two damage types: physical damage (phy) and magic damage (mag). Unless stated otherwise, mundane weapons and unarmed attacks deal physical damage, and spells deal magic damage.\n\n#### RESISTANCE, IMMUNITY, AND DIRECT DAMAGE\n\nIf a target has resistance to a damage type, then they reduce incoming damage of that type by half before comparing it to their Hit Point Thresholds. If the target has additional ways of reducing incoming damage, such as marking Armor Slots, they apply the resistance effect first. The effects of multiple resistances to the same damage type do not stack.\n\nIf a target has immunity to a damage type, they ignore incoming damage of that type.\n\nIf an attack deals both physical and magic damage, a character can only benefit from resistance or immunity if they are resistant or immune to both damage types.\n\nDirect damage is damage that can’t be reduced by marking Armor Slots.\n\n#### MULTI-TARGET ATTACK ROLLS\n\nIf a spell or ability allows you to target multiple adversaries, make one attack roll and one damage roll, then apply the results to each target individually.\n\n#### MULTIPLE DAMAGE SOURCES\n\nDamage dealt simultaneously from multiple sources is always totaled before it’s compared to its target’s damage thresholds.\n\nFor example, if a PC with orc ancestry makes a successful attack against a target in Melee range and decides to spend a Hope to use their “Tusks” feature (which gives them an extra 1d6 damage on a damage roll), they would roll their normal weapon damage and add a d6 to the result, then deal that total damage to the adversary.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/attacking/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/attacking-with-your-companion",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Attacking with Your Companion",
      "slug": "attacking-with-your-companion",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "ATTACKING WITH YOUR COMPANION",
        "lineStart": 1410,
        "lineEnd": 1412,
        "pdfPageStart": 22,
        "pdfPageEnd": 22
      },
      "rulesText": "When you command your companion to attack, they gain any benefits that would normally only apply to you (such as the effects of “Ranger’s Focus”). On a success, their damage roll uses your Proficiency and their damage die.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/attacking-with-your-companion/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/bard-subclasses",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Bard Subclasses",
      "slug": "bard-subclasses",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "BARD SUBCLASSES",
        "lineStart": 505,
        "lineEnd": 507,
        "pdfPageStart": 11,
        "pdfPageEnd": 11
      },
      "rulesText": "Choose either the Troubadour or Wordsmith subclass.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/bard-subclasses/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/beastbound",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Beastbound",
      "slug": "beastbound",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "BEASTBOUND",
        "lineStart": 1308,
        "lineEnd": 1332,
        "pdfPageStart": 20,
        "pdfPageEnd": 20
      },
      "rulesText": "Play the Beastbound if you want to form a deep bond with an animal ally.\n\n##### SPELLCAST TRAIT\n\nAgility\n\n##### FOUNDATION FEATURE\n\n**Companion:** You have an animal companion of your choice (at the GM’s discretion). They stay by your side unless you tell them otherwise.\n\nTake the Ranger Companion sheet. When you level up your character, choose a level-up option for your companion from this sheet as well.\n\n##### SPECIALIZATION FEATURES\n\n**Expert Training:** Choose an additional level-up option for your companion.\n\n**Battle-Bonded:** When an adversary attacks you while they’re within your companion’s Melee range, you gain a +2 bonus to your Evasion against the attack.\n\n##### MASTERY FEATURES\n\n**Advanced Training:** Choose two additional level-up options for your companion.\n\n**Loyal Friend:** Once per long rest, when the damage from an attack would mark your companion’s last Stress or your last Hit Point and you’re within Close range of each other, you or your companion can rush to the other’s side and take that damage instead.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/beastbound/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/beastform-options",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Beastform Options",
      "slug": "beastform-options",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "BEASTFORM OPTIONS",
        "lineStart": 840,
        "lineEnd": 851,
        "pdfPageStart": 15,
        "pdfPageEnd": 15
      },
      "rulesText": "When you use your “Beastform” feature, choose a creature category of your tier or lower. At the GM’s discretion, you can describe yourself transforming into any animal that reasonably fits into that category.\n\nBeastform categories are divided by tier. Each entry includes the following details:\n\n- **Creature Category:** Each category’s name describes the common role or behavior of creatures in that category (such as Agile Scout). This name is followed by a few examples of animals that fit in that category (in this example, fox, mouse, and weasel).\n- **Character Trait:** While transformed, you gain a bonus to the listed trait. For example, while transformed into an Agile Scout, you gain a +1 bonus to your Agility. When this form drops, you lose this bonus.\n- **Attack Rolls:** When you make an attack while transformed, you use the creature’s listed range, trait, and damage dice, but you use your Proficiency. For example, as an Agile Scout, you can attack a target within Melee range using your Agility. On a success, you deal d4 physical damage using your Proficiency.\n- **Evasion:** While transformed, you add the creature’s Evasion bonus to your normal Evasion. For example, if your Evasion is usually 8 and your Beastform says “Evasion +2,” your Evasion becomes 10 while you’re in that form.\n- **Advantages:** Your form makes you especially suited to certain actions. When you make an action or reaction roll related to one of the verbs listed for that creature category, you gain advantage on that roll. For example, an Agile Scout gains advantage on rolls made to sneak around, search for objects or creatures, and related activities.\n- **Features:** Each form includes unique features. For example, an Agile Scout excels at silent, dexterous movement—but they’re also fragile, making you more likely to drop out of Beastform.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/beastform-options/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/benchmark-statistics-for-environments-by-tier",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Benchmark Statistics for Environments by Tier",
      "slug": "benchmark-statistics-for-environments-by-tier",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "RUNNING AN ADVENTURE",
        "heading": "BENCHMARK STATISTICS FOR ENVIRONMENTS BY TIER",
        "lineStart": 11512,
        "lineEnd": 11517,
        "pdfPageStart": 159,
        "pdfPageEnd": 159
      },
      "rulesText": "| Environment Statistic | Tier 1 | Tier 2 | Tier 3 | Tier 4 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Damage Dice | 1d6+1 to 1d8+3 | 2d6+3 to 2d10+2 | 3d8+3 to 3d10+1 | 4d8+3 to 4d10+10 |\n| Difficulty | 11 | 14 | 17 | 20 |",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/benchmark-statistics-for-environments-by-tier/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/blade-domain",
