    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/trait",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Trait",
      "slug": "trait",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MECHANICS",
        "heading": "TRAIT",
        "lineStart": 3355,
        "lineEnd": 3357,
        "pdfPageStart": 55,
        "pdfPageEnd": 55
      },
      "rulesText": "A weapon’s trait specifies which trait to use when making an attack roll with it.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/trait/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/transformations",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Transformations",
      "slug": "transformations",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "TRANSFORMATIONS",
        "lineStart": 2624,
        "lineEnd": 2634,
        "pdfPageStart": 42,
        "pdfPageEnd": 42
      },
      "rulesText": "Transformations represent a fundamental shift in your character and how they interact with the world. These are optional aspects of a character’s identity that the GM can give out during a campaign as part of the narrative or, at their discretion, present as an option during character creation.\n\nTransformations provide both a mechanical benefit and a drawback. Taking a transformation card requires you to buy into the concept of the exchange, taking on the burden to reap the benefit. Because of this, we recommend that players remind GMs of their transformations' negative effects whenever they’re relevant to help fulfill and reinforce the fiction of the transformation.\n\nTransformation cards do not count toward your loadout maximum. When your character gains a transformation, add the card to your loadout as if it were part of your character’s heritage. Consider how this transformation changes your character physically and psychologically—if you need inspiration, each transformation includes questions to help you.\n\nIf there are details you’d like to incorporate into your character that go beyond the features on a transformation card, work with your GM to explore how they might manifest in your campaign’s narrative.\n\nA PC can't have more than one transformation.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/transformations/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/troubadour",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Troubadour",
      "slug": "troubadour",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "TROUBADOUR",
        "lineStart": 509,
        "lineEnd": 531,
        "pdfPageStart": 11,
        "pdfPageEnd": 11
      },
      "rulesText": "Play the Troubadour if you want to play music to bolster your allies.\n\n##### SPELLCAST TRAIT\n\nPresence\n\n##### FOUNDATION FEATURE\n\n**Gifted Performer:** You can play three different types of songs, once each per long rest; describe how you perform for others to gain the listed benefit:\n\n  - **Relaxing Song:** You and all allies within Close range clear a Hit Point.\n  - **Epic Song:** Make a target within Close range temporarily Vulnerable.\n  - **Heartbreaking Song:** You and all allies within Close range gain a Hope.\n\n##### SPECIALIZATION FEATURE\n\nMaestro. Your rallying songs steel the courage of those who listen. When you give a Rally Die to an ally, they can gain a Hope or clear a Stress.\n\n##### MASTERY FEATURE\n\nVirtuoso. You are among the greatest of your craft and your skill is boundless. You can perform each of your “Gifted Performer” feature’s songs twice per long rest.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/troubadour/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/turn-order-action-economy",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Turn Order & Action Economy",
      "slug": "turn-order-action-economy",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MECHANICS",
        "heading": "Turn Order & Action Economy",
        "lineStart": 2838,
        "lineEnd": 2848,
        "pdfPageStart": 47,
        "pdfPageEnd": 47
      },
      "rulesText": "Daggerheart’s turns don’t follow a traditional, rigid format: there is no explicit initiative mechanic and characters don’t have a set number of actions they can take or things they can do before the spotlight passes to someone else. A player with the spotlight describes what their character does, and the spotlight swings to one of the following:\n\n- Whomever or whatever a triggered mechanic puts it on\n- Whomever or whatever the fiction would naturally focus on next\n- A character who hasn't had the focus in a while\n\n**Optional:** Spotlight Tracker Tool\n\nIf your group prefers a more traditional action economy, you can use tokens to track how many times a player has had the spotlight: At the start of a session or scene, each player adds a certain number of tokens (we recommend 3) to their character sheet and removes a token each time they take an action. If the spotlight would swing to someone without any tokens, it swings to someone else instead. Once every player has used all their available tokens, players refill their character sheet with the same number of tokens as before, then continue playing.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/turn-order-action-economy/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/using-adversaries",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Using Adversaries",
      "slug": "using-adversaries",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "RUNNING AN ADVENTURE",
        "heading": "USING ADVERSARIES",
        "lineStart": 4893,
        "lineEnd": 4893,
        "pdfPageStart": 93,
        "pdfPageEnd": 93
      },
      "rulesText": "",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/using-adversaries/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/using-environments",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Using Environments",
      "slug": "using-environments",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "RUNNING AN ADVENTURE",
        "heading": "USING ENVIRONMENTS",
        "lineStart": 11433,
        "lineEnd": 11433,
        "pdfPageStart": 158,
        "pdfPageEnd": 158
      },
      "rulesText": "",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/using-environments/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/using-fear",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Using Fear",
      "slug": "using-fear",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "RUNNING AN ADVENTURE",
        "heading": "USING FEAR",
        "lineStart": 4605,
        "lineEnd": 4645,
        "pdfPageStart": 87,
        "pdfPageEnd": 88
      },
      "rulesText": "You start a campaign with 1 Fear per PC in the party.\n\nYou gain Fear whenever a PC rolls with Fear, the PCs take a rest (see: Downtime), or when an ability or effect tells you to.\n\nYou can never have more than 12 Fear at one time.\n\nFear carries over between sessions.\n\nSpend a Fear to:\n\n- Interrupt the players to steal the spotlight and make a move\n- Make an additional GM move\n- Use an adversary’s Fear Feature\n- Use an environment’s Fear Feature\n- Add an adversary’s Experience to a roll\n\nThe dramatic tension of a scene correlates with the amount of Fear you spend during it. For guidance on how much Fear you should spend in a scene, consult the following table:\n\n| | | |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Incidental | A catch-up between PCs after an emotionally charged scene; gathering information; resupplying at a local market; resting during downtime. | 0–1 Fear |\n| Minor | A travel sequence; a minor skirmish that introduces new foes or signals future trouble. | 1–3 Fear |\n| Standard | A substantial battle with a notable objective; perilous travel that tests might and wit; a tense social encounter seeking crucial information or aid. | 2–4 Fear |\n| Major | A large battle with a Solo or Leader adversary; a character-defining scene with a significant change to a character’s personal story (such as revelation, growth, and betrayal). | 4–8 Fear |\n| Climactic | A major confrontation with the villain of a story arc; an epic set piece battle; a judicial duel to determine an important NPC’s fate. | 6–12 Fear |\n\nIf you find yourself with a large amount of Fear, consider:\n\n- Spending Fast: Spend Fear before the players have a chance to react\n- Spending Often: Spend Fear every time the spotlight swings to you\n- Spending Big: Spend Fear to make multiple moves in a row\n\nSpending Fear to make a move communicates the increased impact of your action. Fear moves often include one or more of these elements:\n\n- Introducing new adversaries to a scene when their appearance hasn’t been foreshadowed or lacks context.\n- An adversary activating a powerful spell or transformation to deal massive damage or boost their capabilities.\n- An environment exerting a strong negative effect on the party.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/using-fear/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/using-spellcast-rolls-hope-and-experiences",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Using Spellcast Rolls, Hope, and Experiences",
      "slug": "using-spellcast-rolls-hope-and-experiences",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "USING SPELLCAST ROLLS, HOPE, AND EXPERIENCES",
        "lineStart": 1404,
        "lineEnd": 1406,
        "pdfPageStart": 21,
        "pdfPageEnd": 21
      },
      "rulesText": "Make a Spellcast Roll to connect with your companion and command them to take action. Spend a Hope to add an applicable Companion Experience to the roll. On a success with Hope, if your next action builds on their success, you gain advantage on the roll.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/using-spellcast-rolls-hope-and-experiences/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/valor-domain",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Valor Domain",
      "slug": "valor-domain",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "APPENDIX",
        "heading": "VALOR DOMAIN",
        "lineStart": 16193,
        "lineEnd": 16193,
        "pdfPageStart": 222,
        "pdfPageEnd": 222
      },
      "rulesText": "",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/valor-domain/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/vengeance",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Vengeance",
      "slug": "vengeance",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "VENGEANCE",
        "lineStart": 1244,
        "lineEnd": 1278,
        "pdfPageStart": 19,
        "pdfPageEnd": 20
      },
      "rulesText": "Play the Vengeance if you want to strike down enemies who harm you or your allies.\n\n##### FOUNDATION FEATURES\n\n**At Ease:** Gain an additional Stress slot.\n\n**Revenge:** When an adversary within Melee range succeeds on an attack against you, you can mark 2 Stress to force the attacker to mark a Hit Point.\n\n##### SPECIALIZATION FEATURE\n\n**Act of Reprisal:** When an adversary damages an ally within Melee range, you gain a +1 bonus to your Proficiency for the next successful attack you make against that adversary.\n\n##### MASTERY FEATURE\n\n**Nemesis:** Spend 2 Hope to Prioritize an adversary until your next rest. When you make an attack against your Prioritized adversary, you can swap the results of your Hope and Fear Dice. You can only Prioritize one adversary at a time.\n\n##### BACKGROUND QUESTIONS\n\nAnswer any of the following background questions. You can also create your own questions.\n\n- Who from your community did you fail to protect, and why do you still think of them?\n- You’ve been tasked with protecting something important and delivering it somewhere dangerous. What is it, and where does it need to go?\n- You consider an aspect of yourself to be a weakness. What is it, and how has it affected you?\n\n##### CONNECTIONS\n\nAsk your fellow players one of the following questions for their character to answer, or create your own questions.\n\n- How did I save your life the first time we met?\n- What small gift did you give me that you notice I always carry with me?\n- What lie have you told me about yourself that I absolutely believe?",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/vengeance/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/volley-of-arrows",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Volley of Arrows",
      "slug": "volley-of-arrows",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "RUNNING AN ADVENTURE",
        "heading": "VOLLEY OF ARROWS",
        "lineStart": 4821,
        "lineEnd": 4825,
        "pdfPageStart": 92,
        "pdfPageEnd": 92
      },
      "rulesText": "**Trigger:** A battle begins and this NPC is involved.\n\n**Effect:** Activate a countdown (Loop 3). It ticks down when a PC misses an attack. When it triggers, this NPC releases a volley of arrows at a target of the PCs’ choice, dealing 2d8+3 physical damage.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/volley-of-arrows/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/warden-of-renewal",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Warden of Renewal",
      "slug": "warden-of-renewal",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "WARDEN OF RENEWAL",
        "lineStart": 800,
        "lineEnd": 838,
        "pdfPageStart": 15,
        "pdfPageEnd": 15
      },
      "rulesText": "Play the Warden of Renewal if you want to use powerful magic to heal your party.\n\n##### SPELLCAST TRAIT\n\nInstinct\n\n##### FOUNDATION FEATURES\n\n**Clarity of Nature:** Once per long rest, you can create a space of natural serenity within Close range. When you spend a few minutes resting within the space, clear Stress equal to your Instinct, distributed as you choose between you and your allies.\n\n**Regeneration:** Touch a creature and spend 3 Hope. That creature clears 1d4 Hit Points.\n\n##### SPECIALIZATION FEATURES\n\n**Regenerative Reach:** You can target creatures within Very Close range with your “Regeneration” feature.\n\n**Warden’s Protection:** Once per long rest, spend 2 Hope to clear 2 Hit Points on 1d4 allies within Close range.\n\n##### MASTERY FEATURE\n\n**Defender:** Your animal transformation embodies a healing guardian spirit. When you’re in Beastform and an ally within Close range marks 2 or more Hit Points, you can mark a Stress to reduce the number of Hit Points they mark by 1.\n\n##### BACKGROUND QUESTIONS\n\nAnswer any of the following background questions. You can also create your own questions.\n\n- Why was the community you grew up in so reliant on nature and its creatures?\n- Who was the first wild animal you bonded with? Why did your bond end?\n- Who has been trying to hunt you down? What do they want from you?\n\n##### CONNECTIONS\n\nAsk your fellow players one of the following questions for their character to answer, or create your own questions.\n\n- What did you confide in me that makes me leap into danger for you every time?\n- What animal do I say you remind me of?\n- What affectionate nickname have you given me?",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/warden-of-renewal/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/warden-of-the-elements",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Warden of the Elements",
      "slug": "warden-of-the-elements",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "WARDEN OF THE ELEMENTS",
        "lineStart": 763,
        "lineEnd": 796,
        "pdfPageStart": 14,
        "pdfPageEnd": 14
      },
      "rulesText": "Play the Warden of the Elements if you want to embody the natural elements of the wild.\n\n##### SPELLCAST TRAIT\n\nInstinct\n\n##### FOUNDATION FEATURE\n\n**Elemental Incarnation:** Mark a Stress to Channel one of the following elements until you take Severe damage or until your next rest:\n\n  - **Fire:** When an adversary within Melee range deals damage to you, they take 1d10 magic damage.\n  - **Earth:** Gain a bonus to your damage thresholds equal to your Proficiency.\n  - **Water:** When you deal damage to an adversary within Melee range, all other adversaries within Very Close range must mark a Stress.\n  - **Air:** You can hover, gaining advantage on Agility Rolls.\n\n##### SPECIALIZATION FEATURE\n\n**Elemental Aura:** Once per rest while Channeling, you can assume an aura matching your element. The aura affects targets within Close range until your Channeling ends.\n\n  - **Fire:** When an adversary marks 1 or more Hit Points, they must also mark a Stress.\n  - **Earth:** Your allies gain a +1 bonus to Strength.\n  - **Water:** When an adversary deals damage to you, you can mark a Stress to move them anywhere within Very Close range of where they are.\n  - **Air:** When you or an ally takes damage from an attack beyond Melee range, reduce the damage by 1d8.\n\n##### MASTERY FEATURE\n\n**Elemental Dominion:** You further embody your element. While Channeling, you gain the following benefit:\n\n  - **Fire:** You gain a +1 bonus to your Proficiency for attacks and spells that deal damage.\n  - **Earth:** When you would mark Hit Points, roll a d6 per Hit Point marked. For each result of 6, reduce the number of Hit Points you mark by 1.\n  - **Water:** When an attack against you succeeds, you can mark a Stress to make the attacker temporarily Vulnerable.\n  - **Air:** You gain a +1 bonus to your Evasion and can fly.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/warden-of-the-elements/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/warlock-subclasses",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Warlock Subclasses",
      "slug": "warlock-subclasses",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "WARLOCK SUBCLASSES",
        "lineStart": 1771,
        "lineEnd": 1773,
        "pdfPageStart": 27,
        "pdfPageEnd": 27
      },
      "rulesText": "Choose either the Pact of the Endless or Pact of the Wrathful subclass.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/warlock-subclasses/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/warrior-subclasses",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Warrior Subclasses",
      "slug": "warrior-subclasses",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "WARRIOR SUBCLASSES",
        "lineStart": 1871,
        "lineEnd": 1873,
        "pdfPageStart": 28,
        "pdfPageEnd": 28
      },
      "rulesText": "Choose either the Call of the Brave or Call of the Slayer subclass.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/warrior-subclasses/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/wayfinder",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Wayfinder",
      "slug": "wayfinder",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "WAYFINDER",
        "lineStart": 1336,
        "lineEnd": 1372,
        "pdfPageStart": 21,
        "pdfPageEnd": 21
      },
      "rulesText": "Play the Wayfinder if you want to hunt your prey and strike with deadly force.\n\n##### SPELLCAST TRAIT\n\nAgility\n\n##### FOUNDATION FEATURES\n\n**Ruthless Predator:** When you make a damage roll, you can mark a Stress to gain a +1 bonus to your Proficiency. Additionally, when you deal Severe damage to an adversary, they must mark a Stress.\n\n**Path Forward:** When you’re traveling to a place you’ve previously visited or you carry an object that has been at the location before, you can identify the shortest, most direct path to your destination.\n\n##### SPECIALIZATION FEATURE\n\n**Elusive Predator:** When your Focus makes an attack against you, you gain a +2 bonus to your Evasion against the attack.\n\n##### MASTERY FEATURE\n\n**Apex Predator:** Before you make an attack roll against your Focus, you can spend a Hope. On a successful attack, you remove a Fear from the GM’s Fear pool.\n\n##### BACKGROUND QUESTIONS\n\nAnswer any of the following background questions. You can also create your own questions.\n\n- A terrible creature hurt your community, and you’ve vowed to hunt them down. What are they, and what unique trail or sign do they leave behind?\n- Your first kill almost killed you, too. What was it, and what part of you was never the same after that event?\n- You’ve traveled many dangerous lands, but what is the one place you refuse to go?\n\n##### CONNECTIONS\n\nAsk your fellow players one of the following questions for their character to answer, or create your own questions.\n\n- What friendly competition do we have?\n- Why do you act differently when we’re alone than when others are around?\n- What threat have you asked me to watch for, and why are you worried about it?",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/wayfinder/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/weapons",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Weapons",
      "slug": "weapons",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MECHANICS",
        "heading": "WEAPONS",
        "lineStart": 3347,
        "lineEnd": 3349,
        "pdfPageStart": 55,
        "pdfPageEnd": 55
      },
      "rulesText": "All weapons have a tier, trait, range, damage die, damage type, and burden. Some weapons also have a feature.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/weapons/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/western-campaigns",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Western Campaigns",
      "slug": "western-campaigns",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "SUPPLEMENTAL CAMPAIGN MECHANICS",
        "heading": "WESTERN CAMPAIGNS",
        "lineStart": 14007,
        "lineEnd": 14030,
        "pdfPageStart": 197,
        "pdfPageEnd": 197
      },
      "rulesText": "You can use the following mechanics in a western-themed campaign.\n\n#### WEAPONS & LOOT\n\n##### Primary Weapons\n\n| Name | Trait | Range | Damage | Burden | Feature |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Revolver | Finesse | Far | Tier 1: d8+1 phy<br>Tier 2: d8+4 phy<br>Tier 3: d8+7 phy<br>Tier 4: d8+10 phy | One-Handed | Six Shot: Place 6 Ammo tokens on your character sheet. Spend 1 Ammo token to make an attack. You can mark a Stress to regain spent Ammo tokens. |\n| Rifle | Agility | Very Far | Tier 1: d8+2 phy<br>Tier 2: d8+5 phy<br>Tier 3: d8+8 phy<br>Tier 4: d8+11 phy | Two-Handed | Sightline: Spend 2 Hope to gain advantage on an attack roll. |\n| Shotgun | Strength | Very Close | Tier 1: d6+2 phy<br>Tier 2: d6+5 phy<br>Tier 3: d6+8 phy<br>Tier 4: d6+11 phy | Two-Handed | Scattershot: When you make an attack, target all creatures in front of you within range. |\n\n##### Secondary Weapons\n\n| Name | Trait | Range | Damage | Burden | Feature |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Lasso | Agility | Very Close | Tier 1: d4 phy<br>Tier 2: d4+3 phy<br>Tier 3: d4+6 phy<br>Tier 4: d4+9 phy | One-Handed | Roped: On a successful attack, you can temporarily Rope the target instead of dealing damage. While Roped, the target is Restrained and Vulnerable, but you must remain within Very Close range of the target. When the target would clear this condition, you can make a Strength Reaction Roll. On a success, they remain Roped. |\n| Small Revolver | Finesse | Far | Tier 1: d6 phy<br>Tier 2: d6+3 phy<br>Tier 3: d6+6 phy<br>Tier 4: d6+9 phy | One-Handed | Quick Shot: Spend 2 Hope to gain a +4 bonus to primary weapon damage. |\n\nYou can also make the following consumable available in a western-themed campaign:\n\n> Dynamite: (Consumable) You can light this dynamite and toss it within Close range. All creatures within Very Close range of where the dynamite lands must make a Reaction Roll (14). Targets who fail take 1d20+5 physical damage. Targets who succeed must mark a Stress. Dynamite deals double damage to inanimate objects or structures.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/western-campaigns/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/when-to-make-a-move",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "When to Make a Move",
      "slug": "when-to-make-a-move",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "RUNNING AN ADVENTURE",
        "heading": "WHEN TO MAKE A MOVE",
        "lineStart": 4518,
        "lineEnd": 4528,
        "pdfPageStart": 86,
        "pdfPageEnd": 86
      },
      "rulesText": "The GM can make a GM move whenever you want, but the frequency and severity depends on the type of story you’re telling, the actions your players take, and the tone of the session you’re running.\n\nMake a GM move when the players:\n\n- Roll with Fear\n- Fail an action roll\n- Do something that has unavoidable consequences\n- Give you a “golden opportunity” (an opening that demands an immediate response)\n- Look to you for what happens next",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/when-to-make-a-move/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/winged-beast",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Winged Beast",
      "slug": "winged-beast",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "WINGED BEAST",
        "lineStart": 1015,
        "lineEnd": 1027,
        "pdfPageStart": 17,
        "pdfPageEnd": 17
      },
      "rulesText": "*(Hawk, Owl, Raven, etc.)*\n\n*Finesse +1 | Evasion +3*\n\n*Melee Finesse d4+2 phy*\n\n**Gain advantage on:** deceive, locate, scare\n\n**Bird’s-Eye View:** You can fly at will. Once per rest while you are airborne, you can ask the GM a question about the scene below you without needing to roll. The first time a character makes a roll to act on this information, they gain advantage on the roll.\n\n**Hollow Bones:** You gain a −2 penalty to your damage thresholds.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/winged-beast/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/winged-sentinel",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Winged Sentinel",
      "slug": "winged-sentinel",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "WINGED SENTINEL",
        "lineStart": 1586,
        "lineEnd": 1627,
        "pdfPageStart": 24,
        "pdfPageEnd": 25
      },
      "rulesText": "Play the Winged Sentinel if you want to take flight and strike crushing blows from the sky.\n\n##### SPELLCAST TRAIT\n\nStrength\n\n##### FOUNDATION FEATURE\n\n**Wings of Light:** You can fly. While flying, you can do the following:\n\n- Mark a Stress to pick up and carry another willing creature approximately your size or smaller.\n- Spend a Hope to deal an extra 1d8 damage on a successful attack.\n\n##### SPECIALIZATION FEATURE\n\n**Ethereal Visage:** Your supernatural visage strikes awe and fear. While flying, you have advantage on Presence Rolls. When you succeed with Hope on a Presence Roll, you can remove a Fear from the GM’s Fear pool instead of gaining Hope.\n\n##### MASTERY FEATURES\n\n**Ascendant:** Gain a permanent +4 bonus to your Severe damage threshold.\n\n**Power of the Gods:** While flying, you deal an extra 1d12 damage instead of 1d8 from your “Wings of Light” feature.\n\n##### BACKGROUND QUESTIONS\n\nAnswer any of the following background questions. You can also create your own questions.\n\n- Which god did you devote yourself to? What incredible feat did they perform for you in a moment of desperation?\n- How did your appearance change after taking your oath?\n- In what strange or unique way do you communicate with your god?\n\n##### CONNECTIONS\n\nAsk your fellow players one of the following questions for their character to answer, or create your own questions.\n\n- What promise did you make me agree to, should you die on the battlefield?\n- Why do you ask me so many questions about my god?\n- You’ve told me to protect one member of our party above all others, even yourself. Who are they and why?",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/winged-sentinel/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/witch-subclasses",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Witch Subclasses",
      "slug": "witch-subclasses",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "WITCH SUBCLASSES",
        "lineStart": 1958,
        "lineEnd": 1960,
        "pdfPageStart": 29,
        "pdfPageEnd": 29
      },
      "rulesText": "Choose either the Hedge or Moon subclass.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/witch-subclasses/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/wizard-subclasses",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Wizard Subclasses",
      "slug": "wizard-subclasses",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "WIZARD SUBCLASSES",
        "lineStart": 2063,
        "lineEnd": 2065,
        "pdfPageStart": 31,
        "pdfPageEnd": 31
      },
      "rulesText": "Choose either the School of Knowledge or School of War subclass.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/wizard-subclasses/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/wordsmith",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Wordsmith",
      "slug": "wordsmith",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "WORDSMITH",
        "lineStart": 533,
        "lineEnd": 573,
        "pdfPageStart": 11,
        "pdfPageEnd": 11
      },
      "rulesText": "Play the Wordsmith if you want to use clever wordplay and captivate crowds.\n\n##### SPELLCAST TRAIT\n\nPresence\n\n##### FOUNDATION FEATURES\n\n**Rousing Speech:** Once per long rest, you can give a heartfelt, inspiring speech. All allies within Far range clear 2 Stress.\n\n**Heart of a Poet:** After you make an action roll to impress, persuade, or offend someone, you can spend a Hope to add a d4 to the roll.\n\n##### SPECIALIZATION FEATURE\n\nEloquent. Your moving words boost morale. Once per session, when you encourage an ally, you can do one of the following:\n\n  - Allow them to find a mundane object or tool they need.\n  - Help an Ally without spending Hope.\n  - Give them an additional downtime move during their next rest.\n\n##### MASTERY FEATURE\n\nEpic Poetry. Your Rally Die increases to a d10. Additionally, when you Help an Ally, you can narrate the moment as if you were writing the tale of their heroism in a memoir. When you do, roll a d10 as your advantage die.\n\n##### BACKGROUND QUESTIONS\n\nAnswer any of the following background questions. You can also create your own questions.\n\n- Who from your community taught you to have such confidence in yourself?\n- You were in love once. Who did you adore, and how did they hurt you?\n- You’ve always looked up to another bard. Who are they, and why do you idolize them?\n\n##### CONNECTIONS\n\nAsk your fellow players one of the following questions for their character to answer, or create your own questions.\n\n- What made you realize we were going to be such good friends?\n- What do I do that annoys you?\n- Why do you grab my hand at night?",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/wordsmith/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/rules/working-with-your-companion",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Working with Your Companion",
      "slug": "working-with-your-companion",
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "CORE MATERIALS",
        "heading": "WORKING WITH YOUR COMPANION",
        "lineStart": 1400,
        "lineEnd": 1402,
        "pdfPageStart": 21,
        "pdfPageEnd": 21
      },
      "rulesText": "The following sections will run you through the basics of working with your companion.",
      "htmlPage": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/working-with-your-companion/"
      },
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/objects/sources/daggerheart-srd-2-0"
      }
    }
  ]
}
